Here's a JavaScript function that accepts text and posts messages via the Slack API to a specified channel:

```javascript
function postToSlack(text, channel) {
  const webhookUrl = `https://hooks.slack.com/services/XXXX/XXXX/XXXX`; // Replace with your Slack webhook URL
  const payload = {
    channel,
    text
  };

  fetch(webhookUrl, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(payload)
  })
  .then(response => response.json())
  .catch(error => console.error('Error posting to Slack:', error));
}

// Example usage
postToSlack('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

Replace `XXXX`, `XXXX`, and `XXXX` with your actual Slack webhook URL, channel name, and token respectively.

