Here's a simple React utility to remove widows. This component will check if there are any words that are too long and break them into smaller ones to avoid widows.

```javascript
import React, { useRef } from 'react';

const RemoveWidows = ({ text }) => {
  const textRef = useRef(null);

  const handleTextChange = () => {
    const text = textRef.current.value;
    const words = text.split(' ');
    const maxWidth = 100; // Adjust this value based on your desired maximum width

    const newText = words.map((word) => {
      if (word.length > maxWidth) {
        return word.slice(0, maxWidth) + '\n';
      }
      return word;
    }).join(' ');

    textRef.current.value = newText;
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <textarea ref={textRef} value={text} onChange={handleTextChange} />
    </div>
  );
};

export default RemoveWidows;
```

To use this component, simply import it and pass in the text you want to check for widows:

